// The knowledge base's statement of MAGE's meaning: the IR ops, their
// families, the layer names that lower to them, the types and the effects.
//
// Generated once on 2026-10-30 from MAGE_ONTOLOGY.json (`sections`: `ir_ops`,
// `op_families`, `types`, `effects`), from the arms of `layer_name_to_op` in
// prototype/src/abl_bridge.rs, and from the opcodes in
// RecursiveMachineIntelligence/src/lang/op.rs. From here on this file is the
// statement: the code is held to it, not the other way round.
//
// The tests that hold the code to this file are in prototype/src/ontology.rs
// (`every_op_has_a_fact_and_every_fact_an_op`, `every_op_family_is_stated`,
// `every_layer_spelling_is_stated`, `every_type_and_effect_is_stated`), in both
// directions. Every name and value is a quoted string; order is not meaningful.

